00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:06.000
And we found that when we treated codependency dependency successfully when we treated this

305
00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:10.000
problem, guess what we lost?

306
00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:12.000
The relationship.

307
00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:15.000
The codependent person would go, I'm a good person.

308
00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:17.000
I don't need you and why am I here?

309
00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:18.000
And it leaves.

310
00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:23.000
So we'd solve the problem but lose the relationship, real common.

311
00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.000
Okay, turn the page.

312
00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:30.000
Let's talk about manipulation.

313
00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.000
What's the definition of manipulation?

314
00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:37.000
The abuser gets a significant other to do things for him or her that are not in the

315
00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:43.000
best interest of the significant other.

316
00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:48.000
The nature of the act is dangerous or harmful.

317
00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:53.000
What goes in the blanks is interest and harmful.

318
00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:57.000
Interest and harmful.

319
00:15:57.000 --> 00:16:02.000
So how is this like dependency?

320
00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:10.000
How is manipulation like dependency?

321
00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:15.000
Yeah, in both situations the abuser is getting the other person to do something for them.

322
00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:21.000
Then how in the world do you tell the difference between those two things?

323
00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.000
What's that?

324
00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:26.000
Well, neutral versus negative.

325
00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:29.000
Look at what they're being asked to do.

326
00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:36.000
If what the significant other is being asked to do is neutral, no big deal, no harm done,

327
00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:40.000
no harm no foul, it's simply dependency, codependency.

328
00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:47.000
If what the significant other is being asked to do is inherently harmful or dangerous to

329
00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:53.000
the significant other, that person is being manipulated.

330
00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:55.000
So let me give you two examples.

331
00:16:55.000 --> 00:17:03.000
You tell me which one is denial, which one is dependency and which one is manipulation.

332
00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:16.000
A 49-year-old alcoholic gets her 17-year-old daughter to go to the store and buy alcohol for her.

333
00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:19.000
That is what?

334
00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:29.000
Well, because a 17-year-old go on and buy an alcohol is illegal in the state of Ohio.

335
00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:31.000
So it is illegal.

336
00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:34.000
So she's being asked to do something illegal.

337
00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:36.000
Now what about this?

338
00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:46.000
A 49-year-old alcoholic asks her 50-year-old husband to go to the store and buy alcohol for her.

339
00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:49.000
What is that an example?

340
00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:52.000
Why is it dependent? It's the same thing, buying alcohol.

341
00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:55.000
She's really not. She knows he has a problem.

342
00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:57.000
I mean, well, and she's of age.

343
00:17:57.000 --> 00:18:02.000
How harmful is it for a 50-year-old man to go to a store and buy alcohol?

344
00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:04.000
Any harm? No.

345
00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:07.000
So that's simply dependency.

346
00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:12.000
But when the 17-year-old goes to buy alcohol, that's illegal.

347
00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:16.000
There's harm. That's manipulation.

348
00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:18.000
Let me give you an example.

349
00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:24.000
Tuesday evening or last Friday evening.

350
00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:28.000
Remember Tuesday, last Friday, around here?

351
00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:30.000
Okay.

352
00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.000
Your neighbor calls you.

353
00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:34.000
No, your brother calls you.

354
00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:37.000
Sister-in-law calls you.

355
00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:45.000
Would you pick up little Billy from basketball practice at school

356
00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:49.000
